## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical data ingestion with common AWS data-lake patterns: JSON flattening, Parquet storage, partitioning, and cataloging. It also covers data quality checks and end-to-end validation, which are core in real pipelines.

## Key Concepts
- AWS Glue ETL and DynamicFrame usage
- Job bookmarks for idempotency
- Flattening nested JSON and exploding arrays
- Parquet partitioning by date and Glue Data Catalog registration
- Data quality: manifest parity, row counts, deduplication keys

